ATTRIBUTION
-----------

Marginalia began as an import of "textbook_quality" by Vik Paruchuri:

    https://github.com/VikParuchuri/textbook_quality
    Copyright (c) 2023 Vikas Paruchuri
    Licensed under the MIT License

As the MIT License requires, the original copyright notice and permission
notice are kept, unchanged, in the LICENSE file alongside our own.

Parts of Marginalia are derived from textbook_quality, including:

  - the design of the course-generation pipeline (topic -> outline ->
    research notes -> section-by-section writing) and the idea of
    grounding generated lessons in retrieved research notes;
  - the model of a lesson as a sequence of typed content blocks
    (text, example, exercise, ...), and parts of the prompt wording used to
    write them;
  - the database layer: the SQLModel base model with timezone-aware
    timestamps, the async Postgres session setup, the Alembic configuration
    and the LLM prompt/response cache.

The git history of this repository preserves textbook_quality's original
commits by Vik Paruchuri. Thank you, Vik, for publishing it under such a
generous licence.


